  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Elevated Technologies Services obligated $309M in FY2026 to date across 192 awards, with an average award size of $1.6M. Elevated Technologies Services' current-year obligations are up 352.9% year over year compared with prior fiscal years. Elevated Technologies Services received $276M from the Department of Veterans Affairs and $28M from the General Services Administration in FY2026 to date. Elevated Technologies Services' largest market is Other Building Equipment Contractors at $284M, followed by Facilities Support Services at $21.3M. Year-by-year obligations show growth concentrated in FY2026: FY21 was $22.1M, FY22 was $36.4M, FY23 was $67.9M, FY24 was $51.1M, and FY25 was $68.3M. Elevated Technologies Services' smaller FY2026 awards include Department of Defense obligations of $4M and single-market entries such as Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $3.2M. Elevated Technologies Services' figures are contract obligations except where values are noted as total contract values in awards tables.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Elevated Technologies Services' main federal buyers?",
        "body": "Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer, procuring $276M in FY2026 to date. General Services Administration bought $28M and Department of Defense bought $4M in the same period. Departments with smaller FY2026 obligations include Department of Commerce at $660K and Department of Agriculture at $172K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and contract types dominate Elevated Technologies Services' federal work?",
        "body": "Other Building Equipment Contractors is the dominant market at $284M in FY2026 to date. Facilities Support Services is the next-largest market at $21.3M, followed by Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $3.2M. Elevated Technologies Services also shows smaller amounts in repair and maintenance markets such as Commercial and Industrial Machinery and Equipment Repair and Maintenance at $598K."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Elevated Technologies Services make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Elevated Technologies Services made $309M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Elevated Technologies Services recorded 192 awards with an average award size of $1.6M, and obligations are up 352.9% year over year. Elevated Technologies Services' fiscal-year series shows FY21 at $22.1M, FY22 at $36.4M, FY23 at $67.9M, FY24 at $51.1M, and FY25 at $68.3M."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Elevated Technologies Services?",
      "a": "Department of Veterans Affairs buys most from Elevated Technologies Services. General Services Administration, Department of Defense, Department of Commerce, and Department of Agriculture are other FY2026 buyers, with obligations of $28M, $4M, $660K, and $172K respectively."
    },
